<===> README.md
Global-only built-in functions (`lighten()`, `darken()`, `saturate()`,
`desaturate()`, `adjust-hue()`) failed with "isn't in the sass:color
module" when called through `call(get-function(...))`. Also checks that a
copied plain CSS function value keeps its name. Expected output generated
with dart-sass 1.93.1.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> adjust_hue/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(adjust-hue), red, 30deg)}
<===> adjust_hue/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(255, 127.5, 0);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> css_copy/input.scss
$list: (get-function(foo, $css: true), 1);
a {b: call(nth($list, 1), 1)}
<===> css_copy/output.css
a {
  b: foo(1);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> darken/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(darken), red, 10%)}
<===> darken/output.css
a {
  b: #cc0000;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> desaturate/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(desaturate), red, 10%)}
<===> desaturate/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(242.25, 12.75, 12.75);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> lighten/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(lighten), red, 10%)}
<===> lighten/output.css
a {
  b: #ff3333;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> saturate/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(saturate), #c66, 10%)}
<===> saturate/output.css
a {
  b: rgb(214.2, 91.8, 91.8);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> saturate_css/input.scss
a {b: call(get-function(saturate), 50%)}
<===> saturate_css/output.css
a {
  b: saturate(50%);
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> variable/input.scss
$fn: get-function(lighten);
a {b: call($fn, red, 30%)}
<===> variable/output.css
a {
  b: #ff9999;
}
